      "body": "The index points to lessons that teach, assume or explicitly connect each idea. Choose a lesson to return to its explanation.\n\nAM–GM Inequality: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p2/3\">P2.3 Stronger statements and unusual inductions</a>.\n\nCombinatorial Nullstellensatz: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p4/3\">P4.3 Dimension and probability arguments</a>.\n\nCongruence: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/2\">P3.2 The smallest counterexample and infinite descent</a>.\n\nCongruence Rules: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/2\">P1.2 Direct proof, contradiction and contrapositive</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/2\">P3.2 The smallest counterexample and infinite descent</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p4/2\">P4.2 Constructions and pigeonhole</a>.\n\nCounterexample: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/2\">P3.2 The smallest counterexample and infinite descent</a>.\n\nDimension Arguments (Linear Algebra Method): <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p4/3\">P4.3 Dimension and probability arguments</a>.\n\nDirect Proof: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/2\">P1.2 Direct proof, contradiction and contrapositive</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/3\">P1.3 If and only if, uniqueness, and symmetry</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p2/2\">P2.2 Induction and strong induction</a>.\n\nDiscrete Continuity: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/3\">P3.3 Vieta jumping and discrete continuity</a>.\n\nEquation: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/2\">P3.2 The smallest counterexample and infinite descent</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/3\">P3.3 Vieta jumping and discrete continuity</a>.\n\nEuclid's Lemma: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/2\">P1.2 Direct proof, contradiction and contrapositive</a>.\n\nExpected Value &amp; Linearity: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p4/3\">P4.3 Dimension and probability arguments</a>.\n\nForward-Backward Induction: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p2/3\">P2.3 Stronger statements and unusual inductions</a>.\n\nFundamental Theorem of Arithmetic: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/2\">P1.2 Direct proof, contradiction and contrapositive</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p2/2\">P2.2 Induction and strong induction</a>.\n\nIndicator Variables: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p4/3\">P4.3 Dimension and probability arguments</a>.\n\nInduction: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p2/2\">P2.2 Induction and strong induction</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p2/3\">P2.3 Stronger statements and unusual inductions</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/2\">P3.2 The smallest counterexample and infinite descent</a>.\n\nInfinite Descent: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/2\">P1.2 Direct proof, contradiction and contrapositive</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/2\">P3.2 The smallest counterexample and infinite descent</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/3\">P3.3 Vieta jumping and discrete continuity</a>.\n\nMarkov's Inequality: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p4/3\">P4.3 Dimension and probability arguments</a>.\n\nMathematical Induction: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p2/2\">P2.2 Induction and strong induction</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p2/3\">P2.3 Stronger statements and unusual inductions</a>.\n\nMinimal Counterexample: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p2/2\">P2.2 Induction and strong induction</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/2\">P3.2 The smallest counterexample and infinite descent</a>.\n\nNumber of Divisors: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/3\">P1.3 If and only if, uniqueness, and symmetry</a>.\n\nPairing Elements to Bound a Set: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/3\">P1.3 If and only if, uniqueness, and symmetry</a>.\n\nPell Equations: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/3\">P3.3 Vieta jumping and discrete continuity</a>.\n\nPigeonhole Arguments: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/3\">P3.3 Vieta jumping and discrete continuity</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p4/2\">P4.2 Constructions and pigeonhole</a>.\n\nPigeonhole Principle: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p4/2\">P4.2 Constructions and pigeonhole</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p4/3\">P4.3 Dimension and probability arguments</a>.\n\nProof by Cases: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/2\">P1.2 Direct proof, contradiction and contrapositive</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/3\">P1.3 If and only if, uniqueness, and symmetry</a>.\n\nProof by Construction: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p4/2\">P4.2 Constructions and pigeonhole</a>.\n\nProof by Contradiction: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/2\">P1.2 Direct proof, contradiction and contrapositive</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/2\">P3.2 The smallest counterexample and infinite descent</a>.\n\nProving Both Directions: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/3\">P1.3 If and only if, uniqueness, and symmetry</a>.\n\nProving the Contrapositive: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/2\">P1.2 Direct proof, contradiction and contrapositive</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/3\">P1.3 If and only if, uniqueness, and symmetry</a>.\n\nProving Uniqueness: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/3\">P1.3 If and only if, uniqueness, and symmetry</a>.\n\nQuadratic Reciprocity: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/2\">P3.2 The smallest counterexample and infinite descent</a>.\n\nRecursive Counting: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p2/2\">P2.2 Induction and strong induction</a>.\n\nRoot: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/3\">P3.3 Vieta jumping and discrete continuity</a>.\n\nStrengthening the Hypothesis: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p2/3\">P2.3 Stronger statements and unusual inductions</a>.\n\nStrong Induction: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p2/2\">P2.2 Induction and strong induction</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/2\">P3.2 The smallest counterexample and infinite descent</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p4/2\">P4.2 Constructions and pigeonhole</a>.\n\nTelescoping Sums: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p2/3\">P2.3 Stronger statements and unusual inductions</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p4/2\">P4.2 Constructions and pigeonhole</a>.\n\nThe Extremal Principle: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/2\">P3.2 The smallest counterexample and infinite descent</a>.\n\nThe Probabilistic Method: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p4/3\">P4.3 Dimension and probability arguments</a>.\n\nTiling a Board: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p2/3\">P2.3 Stronger statements and unusual inductions</a>.\n\nVariable: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/3\">P1.3 If and only if, uniqueness, and symmetry</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/2\">P3.2 The smallest counterexample and infinite descent</a>; <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/3\">P3.3 Vieta jumping and discrete continuity</a>.\n\nVieta Jumping: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/3\">P3.3 Vieta jumping and discrete continuity</a>.\n\nVieta's Formulas (Quadratic): <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p3/3\">P3.3 Vieta jumping and discrete continuity</a>.\n\nWithout Loss of Generality: <a href=\"#/learn/olympiad-proofs/p1/3\">P1.3 If and only if, uniqueness, and symmetry</a>."
