      "body": "Olympiad Proofs is written for Competition Math Reference. Its lesson explanations and original exercises are written for this project. The reference cards hold the full statements and conditions of named results; a name in the index is a route back to the lessons that use it, rather than a claim of original discovery.\n\nContest exercises are credited to their original competitions. AMC and AIME statements and figures are copyright the Mathematical Association of America, used under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Most are imported from LIVE by Po-Shen Loh; some retain PDF, Art of Problem Solving Wiki or Random Math provenance. Answer-key checks also use Think Academy where recorded. Per-paper provenance remains in the problem data. Settings → Credits and attribution has the source links and license details.\n\nFor further reading, the <a href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/Main_Page\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Art of Problem Solving Wiki</a> provides mathematical articles and additional contest solutions. This is a further-reading recommendation; it does not imply that the lesson prose was copied from that source. Mathematics is rendered with the vendored KaTeX library; its license and notices are retained in vendor/katex.\n\nThis book's index and glossary reflect its current lessons. Their entries are maintained with the chapter content; they are navigation and reference aids, not a replacement for reading the explanations."
